                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>How much does it cost to build a jewelry D2C website?</h3>
                                        <p>A Shopify Plus jewelry store with live gold-rate sync, AR try-on, and WhatsApp integration typically costs ₹18-45 lakh ($22K-55K) and takes 10-16 weeks. Custom Next.js builds run ₹35-90 lakh ($42K-110K) over 16-26 weeks.</p>
                                        <h3>Which is bigger for online jewelry — India or Dubai?</h3>
                                        <p>India is larger in absolute volume, but Dubai has significantly higher AOV (2-4x) and better margins. Most successful brands do both. UAE also serves as a gateway to GCC (Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Kuwait, Oman).</p>
                                        <h3>What is the best AR try-on solution for jewelry?</h3>
                                        <p>For rings and earrings, Perfect Corp YouCamera and MirrAR both work well. For necklaces and full-body pieces, custom WebAR built on model tracking (MediaPipe / 8thWall) is more accurate. Budget $8K-25K for setup depending on catalog size.</p>
                                        <h3>Is WhatsApp Business API worth the setup cost for jewelry brands?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes — high-ticket categories close via conversation. WhatsApp Business API with catalog and payments typically lifts high-AOV conversion 25-45%. Setup is $500-2,000 plus platform fees (Wati, Interakt, AiSensy).</p>
